        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-23T08:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think Xing wants to clear the resolve texture when it\u0027s only partially resolved into.\n\nRight now, if:\n- we create a texture A but never initialize it.\n- start a render pass with texture A as a resolve target.\n  - `loadOp\u003dClear`\n  - `storeOp\u003dPartial Resolve`.\n\nThe resolve texture will only have `RenderAttachment` usage, and its content will be only be filled partially.\nSince original code here would skip initializing the resolve texture, after the render pass ends, it would contain a mixture of \"resolved pixels\" and undefined pixels. That\u0027s against the spec.\n\nNevertheless, the solution here doesn\u0027t seem correct.\n```\nif (syncInfo.usage \u0026 ~(wgpu::TextureUsage::RenderAttachment | kResolveAttachmentLoadingUsage)) {\n```\nwon\u0027t work either.",
      "parentUuid": "8f749148_e8cf0fe2",
      "revId": "9a198b9dfa49a47144da1dcd9b30c47f5ad78a67",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
