      "writtenOn": "2025-07-23T08:26:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not actually correct IMO, `(syncInfo.usage \u0026 ~kResolveAttachmentLoadingUsage) !\u003d 0` means `RenderAttachment` will always be cleared here, it breaks the original intention of this code. The intention of this code is \"not clearing the render target explicitly here\" since it will be cleared using loadOp.\n\nInstead of doing this, can we add this code to [RecordRenderPass](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d12/CommandBufferD3D12.cpp;drc\u003d4eaa7ecc4adc54dc936063562327f3d0c599f403;l\u003d1582)\n\n\n```\nvoid CommandBuffer::RecordRenderPasss(...)\n  if (renderPass-\u003eresolveRect.HasValue() \u0026\u0026 resolveRect !\u003d renderSize) {\n    // The resolve texture also has `RenderAttachment` usage but if there is a\n    // resolve rect, the texture would only be partially filled. In this case we\n    // need to initialize the texture otherwise the regions outside the resolve\n    // rect would contain undefined pixels.\n    DAWN_TRY(resolveTexture-\u003eEnsureSubresourceContentInitialized(commandContext, range));\n  }\n```",
